WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.952
Now we make output cleaner with f-strings.

00:00:02.952 --> 00:00:07.642
An f-string begins with the letter f before the quotation mark.

00:00:07.642 --> 00:00:15.802
Curly braces mark the places where Python should insert variable values or expressions.

00:00:15.802 --> 00:00:20.427
Patient A and age forty-five are inserted directly into the text.

00:00:20.427 --> 00:00:27.247
For temperature, colon dot one f tells Python to display one digit after the decimal point.

00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:34.174
So ninety-eight point six three four five becomes ninety-eight point six in the output.

00:00:34.174 --> 00:00:41.229
The important idea is that good analytical output includes both the value and enough context for another person to

00:00:41.229 --> 00:00:43.150
understand it.
